2. LICENSE GRANT BY TIER
   Subject to compliance with this Agreement and applicable subscription payment,
   ZQX Net grants Customer a revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
   non-sublicensable license to install and use the compiled binary Software
   solely according to Customer's active plan:

   (a) Personal Plan (Free):
       Free of charge for up to ten (10) users on the ZQX Hosted SaaS coordination
       platform (`console.zqxnet.com`), with unlimited connected user devices.
       Does NOT include rights to operate self-hosted coordination servers.

   (b) Starter Plan (Per User):
       Billed per active user seat per month on the ZQX Hosted SaaS coordination
       platform. Includes team SSO, granular ACL policies, and MagicDNS. Does NOT
       include rights to operate self-hosted coordination servers.

   (c) Premium Plan (Per User):
       Billed per active user seat per month on the ZQX Hosted SaaS coordination
       platform. Adds Category-5 strict post-quantum enforcement (`ML-KEM-1024` /
       `ML-DSA-87`), real-time SIEM audit export, and cross-xnet sharing. Does NOT
       include rights to operate self-hosted coordination servers.

   (d) Enterprise Plan (Per User + Per Self-Hosted Coordinator):
       Billed per active user seat plus per licensed self-hosted coordinator
       instance (`max_coordinators`). Grants the right to deploy and operate the
       compiled `zqx-control` and `zqx-console` binaries in sovereign, on-premises,
       VPC, or air-gapped environments up to the exact number of licensed
       coordinators encoded in Customer's cryptographically signed `ZqxLicense`.
       Unlicensed local `zqx-control` instances may be used solely for internal
       non-production evaluation during the built-in 14-day evaluation period.

